+def _policy_file(raw: str) -> str:
+    """Policy file must already exist (reject at parse time, like --project).
+
+    Existence is the ONLY check here: content, shape, and vocabulary are
+    ``load_policy``'s job in ``main``, so an invalid DOCUMENT surfaces as the
+    structured JSON error rather than argparse prose. A missing file is
+    itself the acceptance criterion's "missing policy file" case and must
+    abort the invocation (exit 2) before any session or UI starts. The
+    expanduser'd path is returned unresolved -- ``load_policy`` owns path
+    semantics, and the lexical form is what the operator typed, which is
+    what a structured error should name.
+    """
